[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Spice Modern Simulation DSL Proposal

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: DSL-001
TITLE: Structured simulation authoring
STATEMENT: >>>
The new simulation DSL shall use explicit declarations for circuits, analyses, observables and runs rather than positional single-letter records and in-band dot commands.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Rationale: legacy SPICE grammar overloads device prefix letters and analysis directives. A typed AST permits source locations, schemas, deterministic tooling and programmatic creation.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: DSL-002
TITLE: Interoperable legacy boundary
STATEMENT: >>>
The DSL shall provide an intentionally bounded SPICE import/export compatibility layer with diagnostics, dialect selection and loss reporting; compatibility shall not constrain the new language grammar or semantic model.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Rationale: Xyce documents syntax incompatibilities across SPICE dialects and provides a translator. New authoring must not reproduce that accumulated ambiguity.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: DSL-003
TITLE: First-class result contract
STATEMENT: >>>
Each run shall declare requested observables and emit self-describing, typed, unit-bearing result tables with analysis, solver, convergence and provenance metadata suitable for Arrow and Parquet APIs.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: DSL-004
TITLE: Safe extensibility
STATEMENT: >>>
Behavioral models and device plugins shall be capability-declared, versioned and deterministic by default; they shall not receive unrestricted host-process access.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: DSL-005
TITLE: Reproducible parameter studies
STATEMENT: >>>
Sweeps, corners and seeded random studies shall be declarative values in the language and shall preserve their seed, sampling algorithm, unit domains and failure policy in result provenance.
<<<
